<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>By adhering to a strict sequence of verification, testing, placement, and cleanup, the process minimizes errors, protects assets, and upholds the client’s standards for quality and safety.</span></li></ul>

<ul>
<li><strong>Daylight Delivery Verification Against Original Inventory Bilty</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>All pallets and crates are unloaded under natural daylight to ensure optimal visibility of labels, markings, and any surface damage.</li>
        <li>The delivery team cross‑checks each item with the original inventory bilty, confirming quantity, model numbers, and serial codes.</li>
        <li>Discrepancies are recorded immediately on a discrepancy sheet, photographed, and reported to the logistics coordinator for rapid resolution.</li>
        <li>Signed acknowledgment forms are completed by both the driver and the site supervisor, creating a documented chain of custody.</li>
    </ul>
</li>

<li><strong>Testing of Electrical and Mechanical Items</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>Power‑sensitive equipment is connected to a dedicated test outlet with surge protection; voltage, current draw, and functional indicators are recorded.</li>
        <li>Mechanical components such as motors, actuators, and moving assemblies undergo a brief operational run‑through to verify smooth motion, absence of abnormal noises, and correct response to controls.</li>
        <li>All test results are logged in the equipment acceptance register, and any failures trigger an immediate quarantine and service request.</li>
        <li>Certified technicians sign off on each successful test, ensuring compliance with safety and performance standards.</li>
    </ul>
</li>

<li><strong>Clean Furniture Placement</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>Before placement, each piece of furniture is inspected for scratches, dents, or stains; any imperfections are noted and addressed.</li>
        <li>Designated layout drawings are consulted to position desks, chairs, cabinets, and workstations precisely as planned.</li>
        <li>Protective floor mats or pads are used where heavy items rest, preventing floor damage and facilitating future mobility.</li>
        <li>Final placement is verified against the layout plan, and a visual confirmation photo is taken for records.</li>
    </ul>
</li>

<li><strong>Swift Removal of Packing Debris</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>All cardboard, foam, plastic wrap, and ancillary packaging materials are collected in labeled recycling bins.</li>
        <li>Debris is segregated according to waste‑management guidelines: recyclable, non‑recyclable, and hazardous (e.g., battery packs).</li>
        <li>A cleanup crew conducts a final sweep of the delivery zone, ensuring no stray fragments remain that could pose tripping hazards.</li>
        <li>The site supervisor signs a cleanup completion checklist, confirming that the area is ready for immediate use.</li>
    </ul>
</li>
</ul>

<p>By following this comprehensive protocol, the Pune delivery team ensures that every shipment is accurately accounted for, fully functional, aesthetically arranged, and leaves the workspace clean and safe for operational readiness.</p></div>
